{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: archive capacity deferral at exact head f13e261bf814a27e4058cb4a4944f5548a1513d3, tree d7e7e55af8a1e41cd5ae782efcb04068472ed193 (review request 8d0ad68c, promise e955c771, implementation 21a4ab15 / 3c807d35). The head is a child of the slice A head ee8a3228, which is now Main 9d53b9e7, and merging it into Main gives exactly its tree. It may land. Deployment is planner-owned, and so is any operator restart of a stopped row. Please read the residual risk below before either.\n\nRead order: I read the primary, notes/implementation/2026-10-24-archive-capacity-deferral.md (artifact 09c92d5e), first and in full. Then I read the diff from ee8a3228: archive-adaptive.ts, archive-driver.ts, the three new test cases and the seal change. For the semantics I read ArchiveBudget.lookahead and lookaheadAsync in archive-budget.ts, ArchiveRows.defer, wake and #wake in archive-row.ts, and the driver's pre-Mark defer, #later and run.\n\nWhat changed. The branch starts at f8bed579 and 912454c1 (the change and the fixture-lifetime fix), merges ee8a3228 at ba87fd67, records the gate at 163baaf (tree c27fa919) and adds only the note at f13e261b (23 insertions, 4 deletions). The diff from ee8a3228 touches five paths: 18 lines in archive-adaptive.ts, 5 in archive-driver.ts, one seal value in scripts/security-entry-points.test.mjs, 98 test lines, and the note. The act log holds a pointer at this head for each of the five paths.\n\nRequest 21a4ab15's conditions, checked in the source:\n1. A capacity shortage defers and retries, and stores no stop. The planner sets capacityLimited in exactly two situations: a lookahead returned limited, which only the budget produces when its allowance cannot cover the reserve (the ArchiveLookaheadLimited signal is raised nowhere outside archive-budget.ts); or a finish quote is non-null and canSpend refuses it. Both apply only before any prefix is selected; a selected prefix still finishes, as before. The driver returns retry with reason limit and next = scheduled, and writes nothing: no Mark, attempt, stop, token, send or debit. In production scheduled is set before any I/O (archive-driver.ts:180, rows.defer(#later(0)) for a non-pending row); the planner refuses a pending row with reason parent before this code runs, so a deferral never returns a null next. The stored wake row {pending: true, stopped: false, next} is what wake() reads, and run() keeps the returned time as the fallback. The two witnesses (entries allowance 0 and 1) run the real Native alarm, assert the row is {pending null, confirmed null, stopped null, attempts 0, next null}, the wake index and platform alarm equal now + dispatchRetrySeconds, no mint or send, head unchanged, and spent inputWork above zero and within bounds. After eviction and the due alarm the same head confirms with one send and the shortage budget unchanged. The entries 0 case proves the lookahead was actually exhausted; the entries 1 case finds the actual refused non-null quote.\n2. Each hard refusal still stops. A null finish quote breaks without setting capacityLimited, so the planner returns reason limit and the driver calls rows.stop. The witness makes the real transfer forecast null (maxBytes 1) and asserts stopped {reason limit}, zero finish quotes, no mint or send, a null wake and no platform alarm. Invalid data, parent mismatch, exact pending-Mark rebuild and ref conflict paths are unchanged.\n3. Existing backoff and wake arbitration, no new alarm. The new driver branch calls neither #later, rows.defer, rows.attempt nor Wakes.set. It returns the time the pre-Mark defer already stored. Terminal budget stops take precedence, because #limitedLookahead re-runs check() before reporting limited.\n4. Gate once before review: gate 55739 at 163baaf, verified below.\n5. Exact-head review before the planner deploys: this review.\n\nEvidence:\n- Manifest /private/tmp/artroom-archive-capacity-review-evidence-20261024-v2/manifest.json (SHA-256 c987ef2c): all 9 payloads match their digests. In input-roster.json all 63 path-and-digest leaves match the files, including the 26 raw gate files.\n- Gate 55739, raw folder /private/tmp/artroom-archive-capacity-final-gate-evidence-20261024-v1: result.json records expectedHead 163baaf, expectedTree c27fa919, unchangedCheckpoint true, gatePassed true, child exit 0. before.json and after.json are identical: head, tree, clean status and lock f9d837e2. stdout.log shows all eight stages exit 0. stages/test.log reads \"Test Files 495 passed | 1 skipped (496)\" and \"Tests 3529 passed | 3 skipped (3532)\"; the Node block reports pass 39 fail 0, the Counting block pass 55 fail 0. The two shortage witnesses appear at lines 5166 to 5319, and the terminal ledger shows all 17 driver cases passed. The head differs from 163baaf only in the note, so docs/testing.md:597 needs no rerun. The earlier failed runs 34107, 26935 and 31898 stay recorded as failed. The callback gaps (19 ready, 38 result) are kept as a reporting limitation; every affected terminal record passed.\n- Control v3 (/private/tmp/artroom-archive-capacity-deferral-control-evidence-20261024-v3): the mutation removes the capacityLimited branch so the planner always returns limit. Result: 2 failed, 15 passed. Both shortage cases fail at the stored-row assertion with stopped {reason: \"limit\", where: null} where null was expected, which is the named red. The control ran on archive-adaptive.ts bytes with SHA-256 40bff861, equal to the head's, and the file was restored to the same bytes. The null-forecast witness passed under the mutant, as it should.\n\nDocument checks at f13e261b:\n- git diff --check from ee8a3228 is clean;\n- check-commit-messages from ee8a3228 reports 7 checked, 0 flagged; the longest new subject is 69 characters;\n- section citations on an export report 1,877 resolved, 0 broken and 5 known unresolved; the citation script is identical to Main's;\n- merging the head into Main 9d53b9e7 gives exactly its tree, d7e7e55a.\n\nArchitecture: the classification sits in the planner, where the lookahead results and the quote are known, as one boolean and one result type. The driver maps it onto the retry it already holds for every non-pending pass. No new state, timer, cost path or row shape.\nSecurity: I found no defect. No route, authority, credential, gate class or host I/O changes. A deferral refunds nothing, so repeated passes cannot earn work. A stopped row cannot be revived by this path: the driver returns stopped before the planner runs, and rows.defer returns on a stopped wake. The archive-driver.ts seal changes to the maintained parser's value, and the entry-point Node block passed in the gate on identical bytes. The resource cost of repeated deferrals is below, under residual risk.\nSimplification: 23 lines of production change and no shim. Nonblocking: a deferral reports reason limit, the same word as the hard stop, so a tail reader can tell them apart only by state (retry against stopped). A distinct reason such as capacity would make the diagnostic self-describing.\n\nResidual risk for the planner, nonblocking for this head:\n- Cadence. The retry a deferral reuses is the pre-Mark defer at #later(0) (archive-driver.ts:180): one dispatchRetrySeconds, never escalating, because a deferral records no attempt. The production wiring supplies no bounds (object.ts:170 takes wiring.bounds ?? PROPOSED_BOUNDS, and worker.ts passes none), so that is 1 second. A row whose first unarchived entry never fits the fixed per-pass budget will run one archive pass per second for as long as it stands, each pass spending up to its lookahead allowance of reads and costing one platform alarm. The note says, correctly, that the change does not prove every legal entry fits. Before this head such a row stopped once and stayed stopped. The unavailable retries already share this cadence; this head does not change them.\n- Consequence for Room A (c7a17b72 on dap-grow): the row stays stopped after this deploy. If an operator restart (ea0152b3) follows and the row stopped because its next entry does not fit, the restart starts that one-second loop; if it stopped on a transient shortage, the restart completes it. I recommend a follow-up, not a condition of this head: escalate repeated capacity deferrals, for example by counting them in the wake row and scheduling #later(count) up to dispatchRetryMaxSeconds (300 seconds), or stop after a bounded count with a distinct reason.\n\nFindings: none blocking. No hosted cause, recovery, reset or deployment claim is made or approved here.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:09c92d5ea1454da4cbdb3093908d9d118ccc9530","binding":"assigned","head":"f13e261bf814a27e4058cb4a4944f5548a1513d3","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e955c771d1ba150424f1c5e48825961ee57c5540\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8c8773ccde77d373685d08964fca181cb8c62e1c\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6727fe01eb2d75ac060f2f7a21ab056daf17a94e\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3c807d35b47fa01381df4eb41e7db35f92dcd2aa\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8ab90e40be323e96797bd7895cc0836b11be963d","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}